# <relay host>	<fence name>          TAB-separated, one line per Buzz community.
#
# The host is BUZZ_RELAY_URL with the scheme and any path stripped. Do not assume a shape
# for it — a relay may be hosted anywhere, on any domain, at any depth. Read the real value
# out of launcher.log, which prints the host it parsed for every agent start, and copy it.
#
# The fence name is a directory under fences/ holding that community's .claude.json and
# settings.json. It is yours to name and it need not resemble the host.
#
# A relay with no line here falls through to the deny-all _unknown fence and is logged as
# a warning. That is deliberate — a community you have not granted anything gets nothing —
# but it also means a community you forgot silently loses every tool. Run verify-fence.sh,
# which lists the communities Buzz has spawned an agent in and flags the unmapped ones.
#
# Replace these. `.example` is a reserved TLD, so neither line can ever match a real relay.
acme.relay.example	acme
beta.relay.example	beta
